Package: FADS
Type: Package
Title: Semiparametric Inference for Two-Phase Failure-Time-Auxiliary-Dependent Sampling
Version: 0.4.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Xu", "Cao", email = "xuc@ucr.edu", role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("Qingning", "Zhou", role = "aut"),
    person("Jianwen", "Cai", role = "aut"),
    person("Haibo", "Zhou", role = "aut")
    )
Description: FADS implements the two-phase failure-time-auxiliary-dependent sampling (FADS) 
design and inference under the Cox model, described in Cao, Zhou, Cai and Zhou (2025). 
There are three main functions: fads_design implements the two-phase FADS design, fads gives 
the semiparametric pseudo-likelihood estimator, and fads_bootstrap calculates the standard 
error of the estimator based on bootstrap.
